// `&` needs something with storage. a literal has none, and neither does a call result -
// there is nothing to point at (book/concept/pointers_and_refs_v2.md, "Taking addresses").
//
// the sibling case address_of_temporary.eco covers `&($a + $b)`, which is rejected by the
// lexer before the parser ever sees a reference. these two reach the expression parser, where
// they used to fall off the end of the operand production into `assert(false && "unimplemented")` -
// aborting the compiler with no location, and in a release build falling off a non-void function
$a = 1;
int& $r = &5;
